      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MAGARTEN (1) brings the sharpest last-start line, having won a BM76 at this track by a nose after blundering at the start, and his established mile record keeps him right in the argument. MUMMSIE (5) next choice despite being beaten by GRINZINGER LASS at her past two, with her broader campaign still reading well and Stan Tsaikos returning after winning his only ride on her. The BM70 assignment asks a little more, but she has enough current-season substance to rebound. GRINZINGER LASS (2) was favourite when third to MAGARTEN last week after winning a BM64 from MATRON SAMSING the start prior, so she remains a genuine threat if she holds that form. MATRON SAMSING (3) was only fifth in the same BM76, but her strong track-and-distance record and close second to GRINZINGER LASS two back give her a sound place-to-win profile.",
